      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "Normalization in Relational Databases",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "nqdle5JB7WameLpSaTauU",
      "originalText": "Normalization in Relational Databases",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 120,
      "versionNonce": 1122168559,
      "index": "bBP",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "b792PcXfLUFKpZnwqTeUK",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 2671.5616971158743,
      "y": -1109.8121355428116,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "width": 987.1937194979564,
      "height": 50,
      "seed": 599715905,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1725477307857,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "- Normalization is a process in database design used to minimize redundancy and dependency by \norganizing fields and table of a database. ",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Normalization is a process in database design used to minimize redundancy and dependency by organizing fields and table of a database. ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 98,
      "versionNonce": 2078923457,
      "index": "bBQ",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "o_M1jFhl8huYLCZOUJhCN",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 2671.9804566796665,
      "y": -1051.4810533011928,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "width": 941.4644869903002,
      "height": 50,
      "seed": 1522585409,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1725477316816,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "- The main goal of normalization is to separate data into logical units, ensuring that each piece\nof data is stored only once and in the most appropriate place.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- The main goal of normalization is to separate data into logical units, ensuring that each piece of data is stored only once and in the most appropriate place.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 180,
      "versionNonce": 2123848481,
      "index": "bBR",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "tnb-vGI8Ssck_r2UU5tku",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 2669.000476210916,
      "y": -992.9266445445762,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "width": 1055.4248018566711,
      "height": 25,
      "seed": 661874273,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1725477337135,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "- It also helps you eliminate undesirable characteristics associated with insertion, deletion, and updating.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- It also helps you eliminate undesirable characteristics associated with insertion, deletion, and updating.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
