      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1725478186111,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "- Consider a database table that stores customer orders. \n- If the customer’s address is stored with each order, any update to the address must be made \nacross all records. If one record is missed, the database ends up with inconsistent data.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Consider a database table that stores customer orders. \n- If the customer’s address is stored with each order, any update to the address must be made across all records. If one record is missed, the database ends up with inconsistent data.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
